{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name_unicode_normalized": "shannon, c.e.", "full_name": "Shannon, C.E.", "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2573442"}, "ids": [{"schema": "INSPIRE BAI", "value": "C.E.Shannon.1"}], "last_name": "Shannon", "uuid": "b0a2b6d8-daee-4b7e-b461-0cc06e204bdb", "first_name": "C.E.", "recid": 2573442}], "citation_count": 121, "citation_count_without_self_citations": 121, "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "27", "page_end": "656", "year": 1948, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214808"}, "page_start": "623", "journal_issue": "4", "journal_title": "Bell Syst.Tech.J."}], "citeable": true, "$schema": "https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json", "number_of_pages": 34, "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Math and Math Physics", "source": "curator"}], "author_count": 1, "first_author": {"full_name": "Shannon, C.E.", "last_name": "Shannon", "first_name": "C.E.", "recid": 2573442}, "control_number": 2736295, "dois": [{"source": "IEEE", "value": "10.1002/j.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x"}], "earliest_date": "1948-10", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Shannon:1948nms"], "abstracts": [{"source": "IEEE", "value": "In this final installment of the paper we consider the case where the signals or the messages or both are continuously variable, in contrast with the discrete nature assumed until now. To a considerable extent the continuous case can be obtained through a limiting process from the discrete case by dividing the continuum of messages and signals into a large but finite number of small regions and calculating the various parameters involved on a discrete basis. As the size of the regions is decreased these parameters in general approach as limits the proper values for the continuous case. There are, however, a few new effects that appear and also a general change of emphasis in the direction of specialization of the general results to particular cases.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "IEEE"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "IEEE", "title": "A mathematical theory of communication"}], "facet_author_name": ["2573442_Claude Elwood Shannon"], "core": false, "imprints": [{"date": "1948-10"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2736295", "updated": "2023-12-13T11:11:37.759151"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Bell Syst.Tech.J.", "Bell Syst. Tech. J."]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2736295?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A2736295"}, "updated": "2023-12-13T11:11:37.759151+00:00", "created": "2023-12-13T11:11:35.049757+00:00", "id": "2736295"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1002%2Fj.1538-7305.1948.tb00917.x&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}